---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.vue';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.vue';
import SectionTitle from '../components/SectionTitle.vue';

---

<Layout>
    <Card>
      <PageHeader title="Frequently Asked Questions" description="Questions that are commonly asked"/>
      <ul style="font-size:1.05rem;color: #495265;padding-left:0; list-style: none;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">What is Certo?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">Certo is an open-source platform for issuing, managing, and verifying digital certificates and badges using the Open Badges 3.0 standard.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">Who can use Certo?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">Certo is designed for course organizers, workshop leaders, event managers, and anyone who needs to issue verifiable credentials.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">How do I issue a badge or certificate?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">Log in as an issuer, navigate to the dashboard, and use the badge issuance form to create and award credentials.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">How can recipients verify their credentials?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">Recipients (or third parties) can use the Certo verification page to check the authenticity of a badge or certificate using its unique identifier or JSON file.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">Can I share my badge on LinkedIn?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">Yes! Certo provides easy sharing options for LinkedIn and other social platforms.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">How do I contribute to Certo?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">See the <a href="/guidelines" style="color: #5AB69F;">Documentation Guidelines</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/Schroedinger-Hat/certo/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" style="color: #5AB69F;">Contributing Guide</a>.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">Where is my data stored?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">All data is stored securely in a PostgreSQL database managed by the Certo backend (Strapi). Credentials are cryptographically signed for security.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">How do I reset the database or seed data?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">Use <code style="background: rgba(90, 182, 159, 0.1); padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 4px;">docker-compose down -v</code> to remove volumes and restart the stack. See the README for details.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0;"><strong style="color: #5AB69F; font-size: 1.1rem;">Is Certo free and open source?</strong><br />
          <span style="color: #495265; line-height: 1.6;">Yes! Certo is licensed under the GNU AGPL v3.0. See the LICENSE file for details.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Card>
</Layout>
